<h2>  <a name="fork-break-fix-delete-handson-with-tiger-mcp" href="https://dev.to/loc_carrre_0d798813c662/agent-skills-explained-what-they-are-what-they-arent-and-how-to-use-them-bf9#fork-break-fix-delete-handson-with-tiger-mcp">  </a>  <a href="https://www.tigerdata.com/events/workshop-tiger-mcp?utm_source=content-syndication&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_campaign=dev-to&amp;utm_content=tiger_mcp_workshop&amp;bb=264669" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Fork, Break, Fix, Delete: Hands-On with Tiger MCP ğŸ¤–</a>
</h2>
<p>A coding agent can read your codebase, run your tests, and open a pull request. Point it at your database and the calculus changes: a bad migration isn't something you undo with git, so most teams draw a line the agent isn't allowed to cross.</p>
<p>In this hands-on workshop, you'll wire Tiger MCP into the coding agent you already use and give it a database it's allowed to break.</p>
<p><a href="https://www.tigerdata.com/events/workshop-tiger-mcp?utm_source=content-syndication&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_campaign=dev-to&amp;utm_content=tiger_mcp_workshop&amp;bb=264669" class="crayons-btn crayons-btn--primary" role="button" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Register free â†’</a></p>
